WEBVTT

00:07.810 --> 00:09.400
H-Hey...

00:10.010 --> 00:13.150
Do you think the villagers will chase after us?

00:13.530 --> 00:16.870
I mean, we left the entrance 
to the basement wide open...

00:16.870 --> 00:20.180
Ms. Iima said she would close 
the entrance after us.

00:20.180 --> 00:22.330
Huh? But that means...

00:22.330 --> 00:23.390
Yeah.

00:23.390 --> 00:26.670
If this leads to a dead end, 
we'll be in a lot of trouble.

00:32.280 --> 00:35.130
Hey, doesn't it strangely stink in here?

00:36.810 --> 00:38.100
We are close to the outside.

01:02.160 --> 01:09.880
Spice and Wolf

02:23.200 --> 02:27.200
<b>Episode 24
Path of the Snake God 
and Answer of the Wise Wolf</b>

02:32.120 --> 02:32.960
No way.

02:36.050 --> 02:36.930
Huh?

02:36.930 --> 02:38.220
Th-This is...

02:43.400 --> 02:44.870
This is great.

02:46.750 --> 02:49.310
Mr. Lawrence, what do you think this hole is?

02:49.610 --> 02:51.060
I have no idea.

02:51.060 --> 02:55.860
This is the hole that Lord Truyeo was said 
to have dug long ago in order to hibernate.

02:57.740 --> 03:04.330
The villagers always come here to pray 
when sowing seeds and harvesting.

03:04.730 --> 03:07.290
We rarely participate ourselves, but...

03:08.190 --> 03:10.460
Why does the church passage lead out here?

03:10.460 --> 03:13.880
I don't know why, but it's very clever.

03:13.880 --> 03:16.970
The villagers would never dare enter this cave.

03:19.090 --> 03:19.970
Come now.

03:19.970 --> 03:23.010
If we dawdle here, 
we are asking for them to find us.

03:23.390 --> 03:26.010
Let us head down near the river first.

03:26.010 --> 03:27.810
R-Right.

03:27.810 --> 03:29.020
Let's go, Elsa.

03:29.020 --> 03:30.480
Y-Yes.

03:34.940 --> 03:37.120
This den is real, isn't it?

03:37.120 --> 03:40.520
Yes, though I do not know how long ago it was made.

03:40.520 --> 03:43.920
That basement was made to intersect 
with this large burrow,

03:43.920 --> 03:47.190
and it still keeps going deeper 
in the other direction.

03:47.190 --> 03:51.460
I wonder if there's really a giant 
snake curled up at the end.

03:51.460 --> 03:54.670
I doubt it would be able to nap peacefully 
if the burrow it happened to make

03:54.670 --> 03:56.960
is constantly worshiped by humans.

03:57.220 --> 04:01.780
Well, humans are peculiar creatures 
that love to worship things.

04:01.780 --> 04:04.250
Do you not wish to worship me as well?

04:11.150 --> 04:11.980
Let us go.

04:14.820 --> 04:16.060
H-Hey.

04:25.240 --> 04:27.570
So, how are we going to escape?

04:27.900 --> 04:29.830
We shall head towards Enberch first.

04:29.830 --> 04:30.700
Huh?

04:30.700 --> 04:33.690
We have gone through that town once before.

04:33.690 --> 04:36.050
Since we wish to escape in the shadows,

04:36.050 --> 04:38.210
it is better to have some sense 
of the lay of the land.

04:38.490 --> 04:39.820
I see.

04:39.820 --> 04:41.300
Let me say one thing.

04:45.090 --> 04:47.800
If you show fear, I will devour the two of you.

04:50.340 --> 04:51.800
Turn around.

04:51.800 --> 04:52.960
Y-Yes.

04:55.140 --> 04:56.140
Lawrence.

04:56.140 --> 04:56.980
Yeah.

05:09.250 --> 05:10.200
Don't.

05:13.150 --> 05:16.760
Goodness. Why is it always so chilly 
in my human form?

05:16.760 --> 05:18.720
Just looking at you makes me cold.

05:33.750 --> 05:35.270
Are you hoping for a compliment?

06:07.380 --> 06:10.260
As I thought, my fur is truly the finest.

06:10.990 --> 06:12.760
Tell me if you ever want to sell it.

06:18.940 --> 06:20.600
I did not expect much.

06:21.240 --> 06:22.000
Come on.

06:28.770 --> 06:30.570
This is merely a dream before the dawn.

06:31.000 --> 06:31.950
Right?

06:32.440 --> 06:34.490
Yes. You're right.

06:35.600 --> 06:39.000
Looks like Father Franz wasn't a liar.

06:40.270 --> 06:41.780
Get on quickly.

06:43.740 --> 06:46.010
It will be troublesome if we are found.

06:46.010 --> 06:46.670
Yeah.

07:00.490 --> 07:04.810
If you fall off my back, I will carry you 
in my jaws. Be prepared.

07:07.380 --> 07:08.430
Then, let us be off.

07:32.910 --> 07:33.930
Hold on tight!

07:46.950 --> 07:47.940
How far have we come?

07:47.940 --> 07:49.260
Halfway.

07:52.310 --> 07:54.530
Is this a small break? Or...

07:54.530 --> 07:57.070
It will be pointless if all of you die.

07:57.070 --> 07:58.720
Let us rest here until morning.

08:00.580 --> 08:03.610
Out this far, it would take horses 
a long time to catch up to us.

08:03.610 --> 08:05.470
It will be safe for a while.

08:07.430 --> 08:10.300
Do not sleep there. Sleep after climbing down.

08:16.650 --> 08:18.800
I feel like I have become a mother.

08:24.770 --> 08:25.700
What's wrong?

08:30.130 --> 08:31.780
Is it safe to go take a peek?

09:01.060 --> 09:02.280
Mr. Lawrence.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.240
Are they from Enberch?

09:07.240 --> 09:08.440
I'm guessing so.

09:08.760 --> 09:09.880
I see...

09:10.290 --> 09:12.280
How is Ms. Elsa doing?

09:13.520 --> 09:16.070
Not sure. She looks a lot better,

09:16.480 --> 09:19.050
but she looks like she's been
 thinking about something.

09:20.430 --> 09:22.240
There's a lot of them.

09:22.240 --> 09:24.860
That's because they plan 
to return all the wheat.

09:24.860 --> 09:26.780
There are men with spears, too.

09:28.790 --> 09:30.200
Hey, Mr. Lawrence.

09:31.160 --> 09:36.120
Can't you ask your, um, 
goddess that carried us here?

09:36.120 --> 09:37.260
Ask her what?

09:37.900 --> 09:40.180
To kill them all.

09:42.360 --> 09:45.940
Let's say she agreed to your request 
and went to do such a thing.

09:45.940 --> 09:47.890
She would definitely succeed.

09:48.210 --> 09:53.130
After that, Enberch would definitely 
send an army to Tereo.

09:53.130 --> 09:55.280
We cannot fight every army that comes.

09:55.280 --> 09:56.750
That makes sense...

09:56.750 --> 09:59.740
So, what are we going to do now?

09:59.740 --> 10:03.970
If we get to the town of Kumerson, 
we will be able to protect our lives.

10:03.970 --> 10:06.540
We'll figure out the future after that.

10:06.540 --> 10:07.860
I see...

10:07.860 --> 10:09.970
Let me know if there's 
something you want to do.

10:09.970 --> 10:12.620
Fate brought us together. 
I'll do what I can to help.

10:12.620 --> 10:13.790
Thanks.

10:14.840 --> 10:15.670
What's that?

10:18.520 --> 10:21.730
That's the carriage of 
a high-ranking member of the Church.

10:21.730 --> 10:23.930
Why is a member of the Church with them?

10:23.930 --> 10:25.600
To label the village pagan.

10:25.600 --> 10:27.080
P-Pagan?

10:27.080 --> 10:31.660
Someone died because Ridelius' Hellfire 
was mixed in the wheat from Tereo,

10:31.660 --> 10:33.560
but no one in Tereo was harmed.

10:33.560 --> 10:35.360
Of course there weren't any deaths!

10:35.360 --> 10:37.500
There was no 
Ridelius' Hellfire to begin with!

10:37.500 --> 10:39.940
But I'm sure the Church will claim

10:39.940 --> 10:43.480
that the villagers of Tereo are safe because 
they're being protected by the devil.

10:43.480 --> 10:45.340
That Tereo is a pagan village.

10:47.930 --> 10:48.870
Let's go back.

10:54.460 --> 10:57.210
Let's go a bit farther and stop for breakfast.

11:27.290 --> 11:28.270
Elsa?

11:31.040 --> 11:31.960
Holo...

11:34.790 --> 11:38.420
Are you truly... a god?

11:44.900 --> 11:47.360
I am Wise Wolf Holo of Yoitsu.

11:47.360 --> 11:50.680
Though, I have been called 
a god for a long time.

11:52.730 --> 11:57.720
I live within the wheat and can turn 
into both a wolf and human form.

11:57.720 --> 12:00.930
Humans have worshiped me 
as a god of bountiful harvests,

12:00.930 --> 12:03.360
and I responded to their prayers.

12:03.360 --> 12:07.310
Bountiful harvests? Then, are you Truyeo...

12:07.310 --> 12:09.920
You already know that answer, do you not?

12:18.350 --> 12:20.280
Truyeo is Truyeo.

12:20.280 --> 12:21.540
You are you.

12:30.920 --> 12:31.790
Then—

12:31.790 --> 12:33.350
That question...

12:39.150 --> 12:41.340
is not one you should ask me.

12:46.240 --> 12:47.280
Elsa!

12:51.890 --> 12:52.790
I'm fine.

12:59.610 --> 13:02.660
I will carry on the legacy of Father Franz.

13:02.660 --> 13:05.090
Now, I can say that with certainty.

13:07.220 --> 13:08.720
Is that so?

13:12.970 --> 13:14.350
I will return to the village.

13:15.740 --> 13:16.420
What?!

13:19.190 --> 13:21.450
Mr. Lawrence, I'm sorry.

13:24.190 --> 13:26.120
What's the point of returning to the village?

13:26.120 --> 13:28.040
Even if you do, that village is already...

13:28.620 --> 13:30.100
Even so, I must return.

13:30.100 --> 13:30.870
Why?!

13:35.720 --> 13:38.430
I am responsible for the village church.

13:38.430 --> 13:39.250
And...

13:39.720 --> 13:41.800
I cannot abandon the villagers.

13:43.390 --> 13:46.050
Evan, I hope you become a fine merchant.

13:51.380 --> 13:53.310
M-Mr. Lawrence!

13:56.300 --> 13:59.400
Ms. Elsa wants you to become a fine merchant.

14:00.360 --> 14:03.620
A merchant must be able to weigh 
the gains and losses in a calm manner.

14:04.690 --> 14:06.530
Can you do that?

14:11.720 --> 14:16.720
No matter how strong-minded she may be 
and no matter how firm her resolve,

14:16.720 --> 14:18.870
it doesn't mean she's without worry.

14:20.670 --> 14:23.080
A merchant must be able 
to weigh the gains and losses.

14:23.510 --> 14:25.580
How do the gains and losses 
weigh on your scale?

14:40.970 --> 14:42.520
So, what should we—

14:47.050 --> 14:49.500
Was I wrong?

14:51.140 --> 14:53.450
Was I wrong?

14:53.450 --> 14:55.280
S-Something like that...

14:55.970 --> 14:58.700
Who can truly be the judge?

14:58.700 --> 15:00.410
I cannot.

15:00.410 --> 15:03.720
However, I... I...

15:03.720 --> 15:08.050
To fight for your hometown, 
even against hopeless odds...

15:12.210 --> 15:15.010
At the very least, 
you'll be left with no regrets.

15:26.260 --> 15:31.210
My claws can crush stone. 
I can defeat any number of humans.

15:31.210 --> 15:32.960
I know that well.

15:32.960 --> 15:38.830
No one could beat me in Yoitsu. 
No human. No wolf. No deer nor boar.

15:40.370 --> 15:42.080
So, what about a bear?

15:43.580 --> 15:45.960
Could I have beaten the Moon-Hunting Bear?!

15:46.630 --> 15:48.550
I don't think so.

15:51.470 --> 15:53.720
But if you fought to the death,

15:54.050 --> 15:57.240
I'm sure you would have filled 
at least three pages of that book.

16:02.110 --> 16:04.340
I can't tell you if that would be 
a good or bad thing,

16:04.340 --> 16:07.500
but this is all hypothetical. Am I wrong?

16:09.890 --> 16:11.440
You are not wrong.

16:11.440 --> 16:17.300
If you heard that the Moon-Hunting Bear 
attacked soon after you left Yoitsu,

16:17.300 --> 16:19.460
I'm sure you would have rushed back.

16:19.460 --> 16:22.550
But that's not what happened.

16:22.550 --> 16:25.630
Disaster came while you were 
completely unaware.

16:26.780 --> 16:30.320
You understand how foolish 
you're acting right now, don't you?

16:30.320 --> 16:31.380
Something like that!

16:33.370 --> 16:36.720
That, I know well...

16:48.470 --> 16:52.240
What excuse were you going to use 
if Elsa and Evan came back?

16:52.240 --> 16:53.900
Excuse for what?

16:54.430 --> 16:55.530
Killing me.

16:55.950 --> 16:59.410
In a situation like this, 
if I were a human female,

16:59.410 --> 17:01.660
you would have no right to complain 
about getting murdered.

17:01.660 --> 17:03.980
The murdered don't have 
the ability to voice a complaint.

17:04.420 --> 17:06.500
So, what do you want to do?

17:07.960 --> 17:09.710
I should be the one asking <i>you</i> that.

17:16.840 --> 17:18.140
Just you wait.

17:21.150 --> 17:23.140
Can we not do something for them?

17:23.860 --> 17:29.410
It is too late for Yoitsu, but there is 
yet a chance for their village.

17:29.410 --> 17:31.400
I'm just a traveling merchant, you know.

17:31.400 --> 17:33.980
Yet, I am not a mere wolf.

17:34.450 --> 17:36.210
Poisonous wheat, was it not?

17:36.210 --> 17:39.280
I would easily be able 
to discern the difference.

17:39.280 --> 17:43.160
I already thought of that possibility, 
but I don't think that will help.

17:43.450 --> 17:45.900
There is no way to make them believe us...

17:45.900 --> 17:49.080
Yeah, unless a miracle happens...

17:49.710 --> 17:50.840
A miracle?

17:50.840 --> 17:55.300
I have shown such miracles 
to humans for fun in the past! {Note: From ep 21.}

17:57.040 --> 18:00.540
You said you've performed 
miracles for humans before.

18:00.540 --> 18:04.060
I have said such. 
Will that help us in some way?

18:04.430 --> 18:05.450
Yeah.

18:05.450 --> 18:07.520
There have been cases in the past

18:07.520 --> 18:10.020
where claims of heresy were
retracted because of a miracle.

18:10.020 --> 18:13.190
However, the Church is the one who decides 
if a miracle is indeed a miracle.

18:13.190 --> 18:15.600
They won't accept a minor event as a miracle.

18:15.600 --> 18:19.410
So, it must be a miracle that happens 
before their very eyes.

18:20.470 --> 18:21.770
Can you do something like that?

18:21.770 --> 18:23.680
You, where is my wheat?

18:25.660 --> 18:26.750
There it is.

18:26.750 --> 18:28.160
Bring it to me.

18:34.170 --> 18:36.230
Watch closely.

18:43.400 --> 18:44.330
What?!

18:46.950 --> 18:48.730
This should be sufficient.

18:49.070 --> 18:50.330
That's amazing...

18:50.330 --> 18:52.820
It's truly a miracle.

18:54.680 --> 18:56.250
So, what do you think?

18:56.250 --> 19:00.860
The only other thing that can easily be seen 
with the eyes would be my form as a wolf.

19:00.860 --> 19:03.470
No, this is more than enough.

19:07.420 --> 19:10.250
The only question now is
 if Elsa will accept this method.

19:10.650 --> 19:11.360
And...

19:11.360 --> 19:13.000
There is still more?

19:13.000 --> 19:15.280
Even if we are able to tip 
the scales in our favor,

19:15.280 --> 19:17.630
I don't think Enberch will buy back the wheat.

19:17.980 --> 19:21.700
We'll have to turn 
the returned wheat into money.

19:22.190 --> 19:23.220
Yes.

19:23.630 --> 19:27.500
Well, that's where I'll be able to 
show my skills as a merchant.

19:27.500 --> 19:29.100
I'm sure things will work out.

19:30.180 --> 19:31.100
Let's go back.

19:31.100 --> 19:34.100
Yes. It is much too chilly.

19:42.860 --> 19:45.360
You look disappointed.

19:45.360 --> 19:47.370
And you look amused.

19:57.540 --> 19:58.760
I have a suggestion.

20:08.680 --> 20:11.730
That's the miracle Holo can perform.

20:11.730 --> 20:14.620
Now we just need to figure out how exactly 
to show this miracle to the others.

20:14.620 --> 20:16.640
Do you have any ideas?

20:16.640 --> 20:17.920
I have an idea on the best timing.

20:17.920 --> 20:18.690
Timing?

20:18.690 --> 20:20.440
Yes. Any product should be purchased

20:20.440 --> 20:23.460
when the price is the lowest 
to obtain the greatest profit.

20:23.460 --> 20:27.380
Are you talking about when the village 
head and the others are cornered?

20:27.380 --> 20:28.650
Exactly.

20:28.650 --> 20:30.320
I'm sure we don't need to wait long.

20:30.320 --> 20:32.480
Father Mendez is heading 
to the village as well.

20:32.480 --> 20:33.680
The priest...

20:35.060 --> 20:38.130
I will gratefully follow your suggestion.

20:38.410 --> 20:40.110
Thank you for all of your help.

20:40.700 --> 20:46.140
Yet, even if I show them a miracle, 
I doubt the villagers will abandon Truyeo.

20:46.140 --> 20:47.010
That's true...

20:47.010 --> 20:50.800
I have an idea on how to show 
this miracle to the others.

20:53.580 --> 20:54.600
I see.

20:55.450 --> 20:56.400
That's a clever idea.

20:56.840 --> 20:57.900
What do you think?

20:58.340 --> 21:04.150
This method will place 
the pagan gods under our God.

21:04.430 --> 21:06.620
Even so, will you still help us?

21:07.570 --> 21:10.030
Though I am unquestionably more amazing,

21:10.350 --> 21:16.040
a truly great wolf does not take 
such things as one's position to heart.

21:16.910 --> 21:18.890
If it is necessary for your schemes,

21:18.890 --> 21:22.670
I can act the part of a fool 
with a gracious heart.

21:23.810 --> 21:25.170
Thank you very much.

21:26.220 --> 21:28.310
Will you be all right, Evan?

21:28.310 --> 21:30.930
No problem. If I get poisoned...

21:31.420 --> 21:35.690
Just kill me before I realize 
I'm going to die from the poison.

21:36.090 --> 21:36.940
Yes.

21:37.290 --> 21:40.290
If that happens, 
I will easily swallow you whole.

21:40.290 --> 21:41.440
There will be no pain.

21:45.570 --> 21:49.450
Then, I will leave the monetary negotiations 
after the miracle to you, Mr. Lawrence.

21:49.800 --> 21:51.100
Leave it to me.

21:54.510 --> 21:55.460
They're here.

22:11.260 --> 22:13.430
May God's grace be with us.

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
Episode 25

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
Miracle's Path and Journey's Continuation

23:45.880 --> 23:49.190
Next Episode: 
Miracle's Path and Journey's Continuation
